- **`mapper_test.go`** (`/Users/moncefnaji/code/github.com/mrboard/internal/adapters/gitlabadpt/mapper_test.go`) has REST-side fixtures (`basicUser`, `systemNote`, `userNote`, `discussion`, `resolvedDiscussion`, `approvals`, `mr(...)`, `approvalRule`) building `*gl.BasicMergeRequest`/`*gl.Discussion`/`*gl.MergeRequestApprovals`/`*gl.MergeRequestApprovalRule`, all consumed by `MapMR` tests. For the GraphQL side it only builds bare `pkggitlab.GQLMergeRequest{}` literals inline (e.g. lines 311-312, 335-336, 351-352) setting one or two fields at a time (`DetailedMergeStatus`, `SourceBranch`/`TargetBranch`, `UpdatedAt`) — there is **no general-purpose `GQLMergeRequest` builder/fixture helper** akin to `mr(...)` for the REST side; you'd likely want to add one alongside your thin-query work (e.g. a `gqlMR(...)` builder with sensible defaults for `Project.ID`, `IID`, `Author`, etc., since `parseGIDNumericSafe`/`parseIIDSafe` need well-formed `"gid://.../N"` and numeric-string values respectively).

## 7. Existing GraphQL schema references / introspection dumps

- `grep -rn "resolvedDiscussionsCount\|resolvableDiscussionsCount"` across the whole repo returns a match **only** in `.beads/issues.jsonl` (the beads ticket `mrr-incremental-fetch-3sl.3` you're working from, and its sibling `mrr-incremental-fetch-3sl.9`) — i.e. this is a to-be-verified open question, not something already answered/recorded in code or docs. No hits in `docs/`, `pkg/gitlab/`, or anywhere else.
- No `*.graphql` schema files, no introspection dump, nothing under `docs/` describing the GitLab GraphQL schema. `find . -iname "*schema*.graphql" -o -iname "*introspection*"` returned nothing.
- Ticket text itself instructs: *"VERIFY against the live instance schema: does GitLab GraphQL MergeRequest expose resolvedDiscussionsCount / resolvableDiscussionsCount as scalars? ... Record the finding in the ADR either way."* — so there is **no existing offline way** to check schema support in this repo; you'll need to hit a live GitLab GraphQL endpoint (e.g. an introspection query or the GraphQL explorer) to confirm, then record the result in `docs/adr/0005-incremental-fetch-and-selection-identity.md`, which currently lists this as an open item (see ADR "Fold the two ADR verification outcomes back into docs/adr/0005" in ticket `.9`).

## 8. REST fallback path — in or out of scope

Confirmed in ADR-0005's Consequences section (`/Users/moncefnaji/code/github.com/mrboard/docs/adr/0005-incremental-fetch-and-selection-identity.md:205-207`):

> `gitlabadpt` grows a second GraphQL query shape (thin) alongside the existing fat one, plus an aliased multi-MR discussions query. **The REST fallback path (`fetchSourceViaREST`, `enrichMR`) is untouched and remains the unconditional-full-fetch escape hatch.**

So the REST path is explicitly **out of scope** — confirmed by name-match to your own code: `fetchSourceViaREST` (`gitlabadpt.go:668-703`) and `enrichMR` (`gitlabadpt.go:465-519`) need no thin/fat distinction; they stay as the always-full REST fallback used when GraphQL fails (invoked from `fetchUserSourceREST`/`fetchReviewerSourceREST` via `fetchSourceViaGQL`'s `restFallback` parameter, and from the `SourceTypeGroup` case in `fetchSourceID` which never goes through GraphQL at all — group sources are REST-only today, always producing raw stubs that go through `enrichStage`/`enrichMR`).
